
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   |                         Change Packet Format                          |
   |-----------------------------------------------------------------------|
   |  This is where you can select  what type of mail packet  you wish to  |
   |  have created for you.  It is very important you choose one that you  |
   |  have an appropriate offline mail reader for.                         |
   |                                                                       |
   |  (Q)WK      This is the most standard type of mail packet.   If you   |
   |             are in doubt, then this is a good one to choose.          |
   |                                                                       |
   |  (E)QWK     If your mail reader can support QWKE extensions  or can   |
   |             display 'long description names', then choose this one.   |
   |             Even if your mail reader  is only QWK compatible,  this   |
   |             one will still work fine.                                 |
   |                                                                       |
   |  (B)lueWave This one is for BlueWave mail packets.  You must have a   |
   |             mail reader that is compatible with "BlueWave 2.11" and   |
   |             higher (creates *.UPL files) for this one to work.        |
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
